## SRE Content Requirements

### SLO catalog (`docs/sre/slos/catalog.md`)

| Service | SLI | Target | Window |
|---------|-----|--------|--------|
| **Browse** (frontend) | Availability (successful requests / total) | 99.9% | 30-day rolling |
| **Browse** (frontend) | Latency p95 | < 500ms | 30-day rolling |
| **Checkout** | Availability | 99.95% | 30-day rolling |
| **Checkout** | Latency p95 | < 1000ms | 30-day rolling |

Document: SLI query source (Cloud Monitoring metric or log-based metric), error budget calculation, alert linkage.

### Multi-window burn-rate alerting

Document Google SRE workbook pattern:

| Window | Burn rate multiplier | Severity |
|--------|---------------------|----------|
| 1h | 14.4× | Page (fast burn) |
| 6h | 6× | Page |
| 1d | 3× | Ticket |
| 3d | 1× | Ticket (slow burn) |

Explain why multi-window reduces false positives. Link burn alerts to runbooks in `docs/sre/runbooks/`.

### Error budget policy (`docs/sre/error-budget-policy.md`)

| Remaining budget | Engineering response |
|------------------|---------------------|
| **> 50%** | Normal velocity — deploys allowed with standard review |
| **25–50%** | Cautious — reduce risky changes; increase review rigor |
| **< 25%** | Freeze non-critical deploys; focus on reliability work |
| **0%** (exhausted) | **SEV2** incident — halt feature releases; reliability sprint |

Include: who declares freeze, how long, communication template, link to `severity.md`.

### Incident severity (`docs/sre/incident-response/severity.md`)

| Severity | Definition | Response | Examples |
|----------|------------|----------|----------|
| **SEV1** | Complete outage or data loss risk | Immediate page; war room | Storefront down; checkout 100% failing |
| **SEV2** | Major degradation or error budget exhausted | Page on-call; exec comms | Checkout SLO burn; budget at 0% |
| **SEV3** | Partial degradation; workaround exists | Ticket; business-hours response | Single service elevated errors |
| **SEV4** | Minor issue; no user impact | Ticket; backlog | Dashboard gap; non-prod alert |

